---
/**
 * Brookside mark.
 *
 * WHERE THIS CAME FROM. This is the church's official mark, adopted 2026-07-29
 * from the brand package at
 * `branding/brookside-church/assets/Brookside-Brand-Package/02-Final-Logos/`
 * in Compass. Caleb commissioned it and approved it. It REPLACES the redrawn
 * mark this project carried through three rounds, and it makes that work moot:
 * `emit_all.py`, the stroke-weight comparison sheets and the open "which weight
 * wins" question are all superseded. Do not reopen them.
 *
 * WHY THE PACKAGED ONE WINS, stated plainly because the redraw was not wasted
 * effort and the reason it lost is instructive. Every previous version failed
 * the single-colour test: flattened to one ink, the cross dissolved into the
 * letter and the pair read as a barred-B currency glyph. The church's own
 * original artwork failed it too, which is what the earlier rounds proved. This
 * mark solves it by drawing the B as STROKES rather than as a filled letterform,
 * so the cross sits in real counter-space and stays legible with no colour at
 * all. `brookside-monochrome-black.svg` in the package demonstrates it.
 *
 * THE PATHS ARE VERBATIM. Copied unmodified from `brookside-mark-primary.svg`,
 * viewBox and all. Do not re-derive, re-scale or "clean up" this geometry. The
 * package is the source of truth now, and the point of taking it whole is that
 * the site, the print assets and the favicon cannot drift apart. If the mark
 * changes, it changes in the package first.
 *
 * WHY THE LETTER IS currentColor AND NOT THE BRAND GREY. The package README
 * says not to change individual colours, and the brand grey is #B8BAB8. But the
 * package itself ships `brookside-reversed-white.svg`, which draws the same B
 * in white for dark grounds, so it does not hold the letter constant either.
 * Treating the letter as inheritable is that same behaviour expressed once
 * rather than as two files, and it is what lets the header, the footer and a
 * dark ground share one component. Callers wanting brand-strict grey pass
 * letter="#B8BAB8".
 *
 * The 512 viewBox is the package's own. Callers size it in CSS, so it is a
 * drop-in everywhere the old 48-box mark was used.
 */
interface Props {
	/** Colour of the B. Defaults to inherited text colour. Brand grey is #B8BAB8. */
	letter?: string;
	/** Colour of the cross. Brand coral. */
	cross?: string;
	class?: string;
	style?: string;
	title?: string;
}

const {
	letter = 'currentColor',
	cross = '#E6534E',
	class: className = '',
	style,
	title = 'Brookside Church of God',
} = Astro.props;
---

<svg
	viewBox="0 0 512 512"
	role="img"
	aria-label={title}
	class={className}
	style={style}
	xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
	<!-- The B, drawn as strokes so the cross has counter-space to sit in. -->
	<path
		fill={letter}
		d="M116 68h148c76 0 120 34 120 92 0 41-22 68-59 80 46 12 72 44 72 91 0 65-47 102-127 102H160v-38h109c55 0 85-23 85-66 0-43-30-67-87-67h-24v-38h22c50 0 76-20 76-59 0-39-28-59-82-59H154v50h-38V68z"
	/>
	<!-- The cross. Crosses the B's stem and reads without colour separation. -->
	<path
		fill={cross}
		d="M116 162h38v65h77v35h-77v171h-38V262H45v-35h71v-65z"
	/>
</svg>
